# React Native Nitro Modules
# nitrogen/generated IS committed on purpose (docs/research/setup-decisions.md §1):
# generated code must be reviewable, and `bun run nitrogen:check` guards drift.

# real-input suite evidence: the xcodebuild/adb logs, hierarchy dumps and
# screenshots a failing run leaves behind. Nothing in it is reviewable, and the
# run itself is the report.
.real-input/

# react-native-harness artifacts
example/**/__image_snapshots__/*.bak
**/harness-*.log
**/.harness/
# Machine state a harness run publishes for its own wall-clock gates (D21): a
# load average a running test may read, never evidence anyone reviews.
**/harness-timing/

# T02 bench app
# `bench/ios` and `bench/android` are CNG output: `expo prebuild --clean`
# regenerates them, and the toolchain on a CI runner or another machine is not
# what we want to pin. The sources live in `bench/src` and
# `bench/modules/bench-probe` (which has its own ios/ and android/).
bench/ios
bench/android
bench/.expo
# Local benchmark output: every run writes `bench/results/<sha>-<platform>.json`.
# Baselines that gate PRs are committed separately, in `bench/baselines/`.
bench/results/*
!bench/results/.gitkeep

# Reassure scratch space: it writes the current run to `.reassure/` and reports
# to `.reassure/output`; `scripts/perf/renders.mjs` reads `current.perf` from
# there. Nothing in it is reviewable.
.reassure/

# Storybook (S1): `.rnstorybook/storybook.requires.*` is written by
# `sb-rn-get-stories` / the `withStorybook` Metro wrapper on every start, from
# `main.ts`. It is generated, so it stays out of the tree: `bun run
# storybook:generate` recreates it, and Metro regenerates it on its own.
example/.rnstorybook/storybook.requires.*

# X2 gate ledger: one JSONL per branch plus the logs each run teed. Machine
# evidence, not reviewable source - what a report cites is the committed copy
# `node scripts/gate.mjs export --task <ID>` writes into docs/tasks/<ID>/.
.gates/
